+++ b/PORT_NOTES-plan.md
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+# X-027 port notes: subagent "plan" (branch eap-x290-plan)
+
+`crates/engine/tree/src/tree/eap.rs` ported from reth 2.5.1 (6388aae) to 2.9.0 with the patched evm2
+(`../evm2-x290`). Merged into this branch: eap-x290-read up to 6350b04 and eap-x290-pre at f136392.
+
+## Files outside eap.rs
+
+- `crates/engine/tree/src/lib.rs`: `#![recursion_limit = "1024"]`, as in 2.5.1 (EXP-112). The `eap block` `info!`
+  has 305 fields and does not compile with the default limit.
+- `crates/engine/tree/Cargo.toml`: dependencies `eap-lx`, `frame-plan`, `libc`; the dev-dependency
+  `tracing-subscriber` gets the `fmt` feature (the log-line test renders through the formatter).
+- `crates/engine/tree/src/tree/mod.rs`: `pub mod eap;`.
+
+## Cross-module names and signatures (changed from 2.5.1)
+
+- `send_tx(sink, idx, caller, &tx)`: the caller is passed in. 2.5.1 took it from the recovered transaction.
+- `BlockInfo::from_block(&evm2::env::BlockEnvExt<E>)` replaces 2.5.1's constructor from revm's `Block`.
+- `ProviderFactory = Arc<dyn Fn() -> ProviderResult<EvmStateProviderBox> + Send + Sync>`: the readers use the
+  read port's cache-filling `EvmStateProvider`.
+- `EapPwInspector` and `NbInspector` implement `evm2::Inspector<T>` for every `T: EvmTypes`.
+  - `EapPwInspector::allows_compiled_frames` is `pw_jit_real(mode, true)`.
+  - `NbInspector::allows_compiled_frames` is `!pwnbinterp`.
+- `pw_follow_calls(db: &mut dyn DynDatabase, origin, ...)`: the worker reads through the EVM's overlay database. In
+  2.5.1 it read through revm's journal.
+- `fs_exec_begin` / `fs_exec_current` are kept. ewnear, the prewarm heavy dispatch and the key trace read them. The
+  call `fs_exec_begin(i)` on the execution thread (2.5.1 `payload_validator.rs:1473`) belongs to "pre".
+- Uses of the pre port: `reuse::{set_mode, mode, body_end, obs_start, obs_call, obs_create, obs_step, obs_balance,
+  bal_obs_on}` and `eap_ew::{EwWrites, apply_exec_slice, excore_block_start, exec_core_reserved, exec_cores,
+  exec_rt_on, exec_rt_state, exec_slice_set, leave_exec_core_reader, near_counts, near_prio, near_relax, note_reads,
+  reserve_exec_core, set_near, set_sched}`.
+- Uses of the read port: `reth_provider::acc_filter::{set_use, set_check_every, state, take_counters,
+  inserted_total, load_us}` and `reth_db::mdbx::{LARGE_READAHEAD, set_thread_large_readahead}`.
+- Not wired by this branch:
+  - `pw_keccak_hook` goes into `JitBackend::set_keccak_hook` where the prewarm EVM is built (pre).
+  - The miss probe `probe_storage_miss` (2.5.1 `eap_probe.rs`).
+
+## Removed (modules the brief drops)
+
+Public functions of 2.5.1 that no longer exist:
+
+| Group | Functions |
+|---|---|
+| Calldata scan, sd and fs | `sd_*`, `fs_*` other than `fs_exec_*` (`fs_close`, `fs_count`, `fs_diff`, `fs_hook`, `fs_issue_and_wait`, `fs_min`, `fs_take_rx`), `FsAccount/FsDb/FsDiff/FsOverlay` |
+| Chain | `pw_done_mark`, `ch_count`, `chain_thread_mark`, `pwchain_min` |
+| Split | `pw_split*`, `split_*` |
+| Proof hints and proof-page walk | `sr_hint`, `srpf_send`, `srpf_window` |
+| Mempool stage | `mempool_enabled`, `on_head` |
+| Execution-thread inspector | `EapInspector`, `BlockPrefetch::inspector`, `EapPwInspector::fresh` |
+
+`eap_ew::srboost_end` is not called because pre did not port `srboost`. The `srboost` token still parses and is
+echoed. The switches of the dropped modules still parse and keep their defaults. `eap block` prints every 2.5.1
+field: counters of dropped parts are 0. The `eap srh` line is not printed.
+
+## Behaviour notes
+
+- evm2 runs a callee inside the CALL instruction, so a frame's `step_end` comes after the callee's `call_end`.
+  `NbInspector` keeps the callee's result taint in `NbFrame::call_ret` and pushes it in `step_end` after popping the
+  operands. The return-memory range comes from the CALL operands. Tests: `nb_tests::skipped_call_leaves_an_unknown_success_flag`
+  and `nb_tests::callee_return_taint_reaches_the_callers_return_range`.
+- evm2 keeps database reads in its overlay across transactions, so an `NbDb` placeholder is read back unless the
+  driver empties the cache (`take_state_cache`) before every pass. Test:
+  `nb_tests::placeholders_do_not_survive_when_the_cache_is_taken`.
+- A KECCAK256 input beyond the frame's current memory is not captured for the CREATE2 fit. evm2's `Memory::slice`
+  panics there.
+- The `reuse` beneficiary check reads evm2's `State::loaded_accounts`. 2.5.1 read revm's journal state.
