+++ b/PORT_NOTES-pre.md
@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+# X-027 port notes: subagent "pre" (branch eap-x290-pre)
+
+Source: reth 2.5.1 `reth-2.5.1-x199c` at 6388aae (base 6dec1b9). Files: `tree/eap_ew.rs`, `tree/reuse.rs`,
+`payload_processor/prewarm.rs`, `payload_processor/mod.rs`, `crates/engine/tree/Cargo.toml`. `payload_validator.rs`
+moved to "read" (coordinator, 2026-11-01); this branch does not edit it.
+
+## Interface changes against 2.5.1
+
+- `reuse::run_tx(executor, evm_config, block_hash, number, beneficiary, index, tx) -> Result<Option<Tx>, _>`
+  (2.5.1: no `evm_config`, `number`, `beneficiary`). `Ok(None)`: the stored result was committed
+  (`prewarm_tx_result` + `commit_transaction`); `Ok(Some(tx))`: execute the transaction.
+- `reuse::store` / `store_checked` take evm2's `&TxResultWithState<T>` (2.5.1: revm `ResultAndState`).
+- `reuse::StateHook = Box<dyn FnMut(StateUpdate) + Send>`; `wrap_hook(Option<StateHook>)` wraps 2.9.0's executor state
+  hook. 2.9.0's hook sees only the accounts a commit changed (2.5.1 also saw touched but unchanged accounts).
+- `reuse::begin_exec(block: B256)`, `finish_exec(block_number: u64, txs: usize)`, `body_end(beneficiary_loaded: bool)`,
+  `tx_begin()`, `set_mode(m, chk, fast, bal, bg, bg_pool, bg_tail)`: as 2.5.1 (the `bg*` arguments are ignored).
+- `reuse::obs_step` / `obs_call` / `obs_create` take evm2's `Interpreter` / `Message`.
+- `eap_ew::EwWrites::record(tx, run, &evm2::evm::PendingState, skip)` (2.5.1: revm `EvmState`). `EwWrites::new(lf)` ignores `lf`.
+- `eap_ew::EwOverlay` implements 2.9.0's `EvmStateProvider` over an `EvmStateProviderBox` (2.5.1: full `StateProvider`).
+- New: `eap_ew::fresh_reads(&mut evm)` drops evm2's per-EVM read cache (`Evm::take_state_cache`) before every EAP
+  worker run and non-blocking pass, so each read reaches the prewarm provider, as 2.5.1's revm prewarm EVM did.
+- Moved: `fs_exec_begin` / `fs_exec_current` live in `eap_ew.rs` (plan's `eap.rs` does not have them);
+  `eap_ew::set_near` resets the index to none.
+- `PrewarmCacheTask::transact_worker` takes `nb_tx: Option<&Sender<(usize, TxEnvFor<Evm>)>>` (row 6 hand-over to the
+  nb helpers). `save_cache` takes `sysn: u8`. `PrewarmEvmState` gains `eap` (shared prewarm inspector) and `nb`.
+- `payload_processor::mod.rs`: `prewarms_transactions` is no longer `const` (reads `eap::current()`); `convert_serial`
+  takes `eap_tx` and needs `InnerTx: alloy_consensus::Transaction`. `send_tx` gets the signer and the signed
+  transaction (`*t.tx.signer()`, `t.tx.tx()`).
+- `Cargo.toml`: dependencies `eap-lx`, `frame-plan`, `libc`; dev-dependency `serde_json` (heavy-first test).
+
+## Not ported (off in the final configuration)
+
+- `reusechkbg` (background reuse check): the `eap reuse` line prints its fields as 0.
+- `ewlf` (lock-free write tables) and `srboost`; `eap_ew::srboost_end()` is a no-op kept for plan's `refresh`.
+- EXP-018 per-transaction diagnostics (`cc_diag_block`), so `EwJob::redo` is unread (`allow(dead_code)`). Ported afterwards (X-027, Master 11-02, see PORT_X027.md "Added after 5efedeb").
+
+## Behaviour differences found while porting
+
+- Reuse of a fee-only beneficiary update: when the committed beneficiary would be empty while it exists, the
+  execution thread executes the transaction instead (evm2 cannot commit that detached account the same way).
+- Balance-only acceptance (`reusebal`) rejects an account created, destroyed or storage-wiped in the run.
+- Reuse check mode compares the touched-account list captured at store time (`Entry::touched`), because
+  `PendingState::insert_account` drops the touched flag when the balance is rewritten.
+- With prewarm-result reuse of 2.9.0 itself (`--engine.prewarm-reuse`, off in every row) the prewarm EVM runs its
+  `BalanceTracker` and the EAP inspector as one (`PairInspector`); unused in the configurations of record.
+
+## Rows without EAP
+
+With `EAP_CTRL` absent: `pw_inspector` gives `None`, `ew()` gives `None`, `sysn()` gives 0, `pwheavyfirst` and
+`pwearlydisp` are off, `prewarms_transactions` reduces to 2.9.0's condition (`Mode::prewarm` defaults to true), the
+prewarm EVM configuration is 2.9.0's, and the per-block calls (`refresh`, `sched_block`, `accflt_block`,
+`advance_generation`, `cache_guard_report`, clearing the JIT keccak/balance callbacks) do no work on the
+execution path.
+
+## Shims
+
+None. Plan's `x027_shim_read.rs` is gone after merging eap-x290-plan a3e3cc4.
+
+## Checks asked by the coordinator
+
+- KECCAK256 and balance callbacks of compiled prewarm code: `evm_for_ctx_ew` sets or clears both on every prewarm
+  thread each time it builds the block's prewarm EVM (2.5.1 prewarm.rs:2391-2409); 2.5.1 has no other install or
+  removal point (nb passes and the execution thread never set them).
+- "Beneficiary loaded by the body" (plan's `EapPwInspector::reuse_frame_end`, evm2 `State::loaded_accounts`): evm2
+  warms the coinbase through the pre-warmed set (`ethereum/mod.rs:471` `state.prewarm`, `state/mod.rs:492`), which
+  does not load the account, and credits the fee in `default_settle_gas` after the top-level frame
+  (`ethereum/mod.rs:766`). Test `reuse::tests::prewarm_inspector_sees_only_the_body_loading_the_beneficiary`
+  runs plan's inspector: a transfer between two other accounts gives "not loaded"; BALANCE(COINBASE) and a transfer to
+  the beneficiary give "loaded".
+
+## Tests and the global mode
+
+`reuse::EAP_MODE_TEST` (cfg(test) RwLock): tests that set the global EAP mode hold it for writing, the conversion tests
+in `payload_processor::tests` for reading. Block-validation tests elsewhere reset the mode through `eap::refresh`, so
+the mode-setting tests are reliable with the filters `tree::reuse` and `payload_processor::tests`.
+
+## Kept from 2.5.1 although 2.9.0 differs
+
+- The `pwearlydisp` and `pwheavyfirst` recovery paths keep 2.5.1's behaviour: they do not stop at the first failed
+  conversion or when execution drops its receiver (2.9.0's default path stops). Both switches are off in rows without
+  EAP; the default path keeps 2.9.0's stop.
