+//! EngineAccessPlan EXP-171 (exploration X-014): reuse of the prewarm worker's execution result on the execution thread.
+//!
+//! The prewarm workers execute every transaction on the block's pre-state. With `reuse=` in `EAP_CTRL` they keep the
+//! result ([`store`]); when the execution thread reaches the transaction it checks the result's read set against its own
+//! state ([`prepare`]): every account the run loaded must still have the balance, nonce and code hash it had when it was
+//! loaded (`Account::original_info`, or loaded as not existing), and every storage slot it loaded its `original_value`.
+//! The beneficiary is credited with the priority fee by every transaction; when the run's body did not load it (the
+//! prewarm inspector records whether it was in the journal when the top-level frame ended, [`body_end`]), its read is not
+//! checked and the fee is applied as an increment on the current balance. The sender's nonce must equal the transaction's
+//! nonce and its balance must cover the maximum cost (the prewarm runs with both checks off).
+//!
+//! `reuse=1` (check): the execution thread executes as usual and compares the result of every transaction whose read set
+//! was valid with the prewarm result, field by field ([`compare`]); `reuse=2` (on): a valid result is committed as the
+//! transaction's result and the EVM is not run. Per block one log line `eap reuse` (target `reth::eap`).
+//!
+//! EXP-179: the committed state carries the fee-only beneficiary with its current info as the info it was loaded with, as
+//! the execution thread's own run loads it ([`as_committed`]), so that the state-root task's update of every reused
+//! transaction equals the update of the execution thread's own run; check mode also compares the two updates
+//! ([`state_update`], counter `upd_mismatch`).
+//!
+//! X-027 port to reth 2.9.0 (evm2): an entry keeps the run's detached [`PendingState`] and its type-erased [`TxResult`];
+//! the read set is checked through the executor's accepted state overlay (`state_db_mut`); a valid result is committed
+//! with `ConfigureEvm::prewarm_tx_result` and `commit_transaction`; the written keys are recorded from the executor's
+//! state hook ([`StateUpdate`]). The background checks of EXP-215 (`reusechkbg`) are not ported (off in the final
+//! configuration): their switch is parsed and ignored, and their fields in the `eap reuse` line stay 0. evm2's detached
+//! state cannot mark an account touched without changing it, so a result whose commit would need that (a fee-only
+//! beneficiary that is empty after the credit) is executed instead (counted as `fail(0)`), and a balance change of an
+//! account created or destroyed in the run is not accepted as an increment.
+//!
+//! Prologue (`reusediag=1`, [`set_diag`]): every transaction whose prewarm result is not committed gets a record of why
+//! (no result, or the failure kind of `fail`), the account or slot whose check failed, and the block's last commit that
+//! changed it before the transaction (recorded from the state hook); one `eap reusediag` line per block
+//! ([`finish_exec`]). For an account it also tells how the run observed the account's balance (read, or value sent out
+//! of it) and, when only by sending value, whether the current balance still covers the total sent: what a relaxation
+//! of `reusebal` to such accounts could accept (`reusebal` itself still refuses every observed account).
+//!
+//! Prologue (`reusebalsend=1`, [`set_bal_send`]): that relaxation. A run that observed an account's balance only by
+//! sending value out of it depends only on each transfer having enough balance. The run records, per account, the
+//! least balance its transfers out of it left ([`BalObs::min_slack`]); applying the account's change as an increment
+//! moves its balance by the same amount before each of them, so the account is accepted when every transfer succeeded
+//! and still succeeds after the move ([`bal_relax`]).
+
+use alloy_consensus::Transaction as _;
+use alloy_primitives::{map::AddressMap, Address, B256, U256};
+use evm2::{
+    evm::{AccountChanges, AccountInfo, DynDatabase, PendingState},
+    interpreter::{op, Interpreter, Message, MessageKind},
+    utils::WordExt,
+    EvmTypes, TxResult, TxResultWithState,
+};
+use parking_lot::Mutex;
+use reth_errors::BlockExecutionError;
+use reth_evm::{
+    BlockExecutor, BlockExecutorFor, ConfigureEvm, Evm as _, EvmTypesFor, ExecutableTxFor, RecoveredTx,
+};
+use reth_execution_types::StateUpdate;
+use std::{
+    cell::Cell,
+    collections::HashMap,
+    fmt,
+    sync::{
+        atomic::{AtomicBool, AtomicU64, AtomicU8, Ordering},
+        LazyLock,
+    },
+};
+use tracing::{info, warn};
+
+/// Mode of the block being processed: 0 off, 1 check, 2 on (`reuse=` in `EAP_CTRL`, set by `eap::refresh`).
+static MODE: AtomicU8 = AtomicU8::new(0);
+
+/// X-027: tests that set the global EAP mode (`eap::set_mode_for_test`) hold this lock for writing, tests whose path
+/// reads it for reading. Block-validation tests elsewhere in the crate reset the mode (`eap::refresh`), so the tests
+/// that set it run reliably with a filter (`tree::reuse`, `payload_processor::tests`).
+#[cfg(test)]
+pub(crate) static EAP_MODE_TEST: parking_lot::RwLock<()> = parking_lot::const_rwlock(());
+
+/// `reusechk=N`: in mode 2, every transaction whose index is a multiple of N is executed and compared instead of reused.
+static CHK: AtomicU64 = AtomicU64::new(0);
+
+/// Set at the first difference found by [`compare`]: from then on mode 2 behaves as mode 1 for the rest of the process.
+static TRIPPED: AtomicBool = AtomicBool::new(false);
+
+/// A prewarm result kept for the execution thread. The execution result is kept type-erased because the prewarm task is
+/// generic over the EVM's types; the execution thread uses it only when it is the executor's [`TxResult`].
+pub struct Entry {
+    state: PendingState,
+    result: Box<dyn std::any::Any + Send>,
+    /// X-027: the accounts the run touched, sorted (check mode compares them; rewriting an account's balance as
+    /// detached state, [`apply_adjust`], drops evm2's touched flag)
+    touched: Vec<Address>,
+    /// the beneficiary was loaded only by the post-execution fee credit
+    fee_only: bool,
+    /// EXP-199 (`ewov`): checked against every key it read, also under `reusefast`
+    full_check: bool,
+    /// EXP-199 (`ewredo`): the run number of the prewarm run that produced it (an older run's entry does not replace it)
+    run: u32,
+    /// EXP-206 (`reusebal`): the accounts whose balance the run observed (BALANCE, SELFBALANCE, value sent out,
+    /// SELFDESTRUCT) and how ([`BalObs`]); `None` when the run was not observed (the switch off, or no inspector reported
+    /// its top-level frame end), and then no balance change is accepted
+    bal_obs: Option<AddressMap<BalObs>>,
+}
+
+/// Results by (block hash, transaction index); entries of other blocks are dropped when a block's execution starts.
+static SLOTS: LazyLock<Mutex<HashMap<(B256, usize), Box<Entry>>>> = LazyLock::new(|| Mutex::new(HashMap::new()));
+
+thread_local! {
+    /// prewarm worker: 0 no top-level frame end seen yet, 1 the beneficiary was in the journal at the end of the
+    /// top-level frame, 2 it was not
+    static CB_BODY: Cell<u8> = const { Cell::new(0) };
+    /// EXP-206 (`reusebal`): the balances the current run on this thread observed, and how; `None` unless the prewarm
+    /// inspector started recording at the run's top-level frame ([`obs_start`])
+    static OBS: std::cell::RefCell<Option<AddressMap<BalObs>>> = const { std::cell::RefCell::new(None) };
+    /// EXP-233: an observation of the current run could not be recorded ([`pw_balance_hook`]); the run then stores no
+    /// observations, so none of its balance changes is accepted
+    static OBS_LOST: Cell<bool> = const { Cell::new(false) };
+    /// EXP-233: this thread's prewarm EVM runs compiled code for an inspector that records balance observations, but
+    /// the JIT backend could not install the balance callback; its runs then store no observations
+    static OBS_NO_HOOK: Cell<bool> = const { Cell::new(false) };
+}
+
+#[derive(Default)]
+struct Stats {
+    stored: AtomicU64,
+    found: AtomicU64,
+    missing: AtomicU64,
+    valid: AtomicU64,
+    reused: AtomicU64,
+    fail: [AtomicU64; 8],
+    mismatch: AtomicU64,
+    /// check mode: valid results whose state-root update differs from the execution thread's own (must be 0)
+    upd_mismatch: AtomicU64,
+    fee_only: AtomicU64,
+    checked: AtomicU64,
+    /// mode 1: transactions on which the restricted and the full check decide differently (must be 0)
+    fast_diff: AtomicU64,
+    /// check mode: results equal in the block's fields but not in the halt / success reason or the output
+    nonconsensus: AtomicU64,
+    /// the same by kind: [unused, reason, output, revert against halt]
+    nc_kind: [AtomicU64; 4],
